{"name":"Beyond the Pale","hex":"#f7d6ba","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beyond the pale","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["Of a person or their behaviour: outside the bounds of what is acceptable, or regarded as good judgment, morality, ethics, etc.","Used other than as an idiom; generally followed by of: beyond the extent or limits."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beyond_the_pale"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plain Tales from the Hills","blocks":[{"text":"Plain Tales from the Hills is the first collection of short stories by Rudyard Kipling. Out of its 40 stories, \"eight-and-twenty\", according to Kipling's Preface, were initially published in the Civil and Military Gazette in Lahore, Punjab, British India between November 1886 and June 1887. \"The remaining tales are, more or less, new.\""}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Plaintalesfromthehills1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain_Tales_from_the_Hills"},{"title":"Beyond the Pale (Jarv Is album)","blocks":[{"text":"Beyond the Pale is the debut studio album by British rock band Jarv Is, led by Pulp frontman Jarvis Cocker. The studio album incorporates live recordings, and was defined by the group as an \"alive album\". It was released by Rough Trade Records on 17 July 2020, having been delayed by the COVID-19 pandemic, and received widespread acclaim upon release, with multiple critics characterising it as Cocker's best work since Pulp."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Jarv_Is_-_Beyond_the_Pale.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_the_Pale_(Jarv_Is_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Plaintalesfromthehills1888.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte